    {
      "id": "arpt6io",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 State at a Glance — Basic Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Karnataka is geographically structured into three main physical divisions: Coastal Plains (Karavali), Hilly Region (Malnad), and Plains Region (Maidan).",
        "The Western Ghats (Sahyadris) act as a major watershed and strongly dictate the monsoon climatic patterns across the state.",
        "The major east-flowing river systems draining into the Bay of Bengal are the Krishna and Kaveri rivers.",
        "West-flowing rivers like Sharavathi and Kali flow down steep gradients into the Arabian Sea, creating prominent waterfalls like Jog Falls.",
        "Mullayanagiri in the Baba Budangiri range is the highest peak in the state of Karnataka."
      ],
      "id": "cgw9air"
    },
