    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "SECTION 1: GEOGRAPHY OF KARNATAKA",
      "id": "48k33hg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s4xunc0",
      "content": "Karnataka is broadly divided into three natural physical regions based on relief, rainfall, and vegetation:"
    },
    {
      "id": "yd8j2ng",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Region</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Sub-Regions / Features</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Districts Covered</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Coastal Karnataka (Karavali)</p>",
            "<p>Low alluvial plains, humid, heavy SW monsoon (2,500–3,800 mm); coconut, arecanut, spice cultivation; fishing communities</p>",
            "<p>Dakshina Kannada, Udupi, Uttara Kannada (coastal strip)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Malnad (Hill Region)</p>",
            "<p>Western Ghats; elevations 600–1,930 m; dense shola forests; highest rainfall in state; origin of major rivers; coffee &amp; spice cultivation</p>",
            "<p>Kodagu, Chikkamagaluru, Shivamogga, Hassan, Uttara Kannada (ghats portion)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Maidan (Plateau Region)</p>",
            "<p>Deccan Plateau; 300–900 m elevation; semi-arid in north; black cotton soil; red laterite soil in south; major agricultural belt</p>",
            "<p>All remaining central &amp; northern districts</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Northern Transitional Zone</p>",
            "<p>Transition between Deccan plateau and Malnad; mixed soil; dryland farming; Tungabhadra basin</p>",
            "<p>Dharwad, Haveri, Gadag, parts of Davanagere</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>North-East Arid Zone</p>",
            "<p>Low rainfall (&lt;500 mm); rocky terrain; Deccan trap rock; scrub vegetation</p>",
            "<p>Kalaburagi, Bidar, Raichur, Yadgir</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
