            "<p>Brahmagiri Hills, Kodagu</p>",
            "<p>West</p>",
            "<p>Arabian Sea</p>",
            "<p>Passes through Mangaluru; Bantwal Dam; drains D. Kannada</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bedti (Gangavali)</p>",
            "<p>Dharwad plateau</p>",
            "<p>West</p>",
            "<p>Arabian Sea</p>",
            "<p>Magod Falls (198 m) on this river; passes through Uttara Kannada</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Kabini</p>",
            "<p>Wayanad plateau, Kerala</p>",
            "<p>North-East</p>",
            "<p>Cauvery</p>",
            "<p>Kabini Reservoir (Mysuru-Kodagu border); excellent wildlife area</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hemavathi</p>",
            "<p>Bisle Ghat, Sakleshpur</p>",
            "<p>East</p>",
            "<p>Cauvery</p>",
            "<p>Hemavathi Reservoir (Hassan); feeds Cauvery basin</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Arkavathi</p>",
            "<p>Nandi Hills, Chikkaballapur</p>",
            "<p>South</p>",
            "<p>Cauvery</p>",
            "<p>Passes through Bengaluru rural; Manchanabele Dam</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bhadra</p>",
            "<p>Gangamoola, Chikkamagaluru</p>",
            "<p>East (joins Tunga)</p>",
            "<p>Krishna (via Tungabhadra)</p>",
            "<p>Bhadra Wildlife Sanctuary along its banks; Bhadra Reservoir</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3uqs32w",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><img></img><strong>EXAM NOTE — Waterfalls:</strong></p><p>• Jog Falls (Gerusoppa Falls) — 253 m — Sharavathi River — Shivamogga (tallest plunge waterfall in India)  </p><p>• Gokak Falls — 52 m — Ghataprabha River — Belagavi district</p><p>• Magod Falls — 198 m — Bedti River — Uttara Kannada</p><p>• Abbey Falls — Kodagu (Cauvery tributary)</p><p>• Shivanasamudra Falls — Cauvery River — Mandya; India's first hydroelectric power station (1902)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
